# Band irradiance -- for M02 the TSL2585's UV-A channel, 315-400 nm (M02 spec
# 6.4). Minted because the standard set has no irradiance sample type: the
# nearest, uavcan.si.sample.luminance.Scalar, is candela per square metre, a
# photometric quantity weighted by the human eye's response, which is the wrong
# quantity for a UV band by construction (ADR-0005 d2).
#
# Watt per square metre, unscaled SI.
#
# The value is NOMINAL, not guaranteed. It is the device's raw count scaled by
# the responsivity of M02 spec 6.4, which the datasheet states as a typical with
# neither minimum nor maximum, and corrected by the device's own OTP UV
# calibration factor. The band the figure is anchored at is 365 nm; a source
# with power elsewhere in 315-400 nm reads against that anchor.
#
# The band is not a field. One subject carries one band, so an instrument that
# grows a second UV channel gets a second subject rather than a discriminator
# every consumer has to switch on.
uavcan.time.SynchronizedTimestamp.1.0 timestamp
float32 watt_per_square_metre
bool valid   # true = the modulator converted this cycle and did not saturate
@extent 16 * 8
